{
  "measurement": "Three alternating fresh processes per mode in one binary. Both retain the same 16 MiB parent and construct the same 8 MiB child style fixture via the sink TextRunBuilder constructor inside a helper procedure; copy mode retains that independent storage, range mode retains the parent range. The fixture helper has returned before childRetained. Bounded substring/style reads precede explicit materialization; discardHeld retains a previously returned snapshot, and discardReleased releases it. Live macOS malloc-zone heap, RSS, and process peak RSS; this is a storage-only probe, not Markdown rendering/layout.",
  "attribution": "Separate paused MallocStackLogging memgraphs at childRetained: malloc_history -allBySize reports one 8,388,617-byte requested allocation in copy mode from mnewString -> string slice -> TextStorage.storageSubstring -> childStorage; this allocation is absent in range mode. The call-tree heap+VM view charges the same stack 16.0M and zone totals differ by roughly 16.1 MiB; the reason for that discrepancy is unresolved. A standalone untraced calloc(1,8388617) macOS malloc_size check reported 8,404,992 usable bytes; do not attribute the entire reported heap difference to two copies or ordinary allocator rounding. A parent allocation is retained in both modes.",
  "platform": "macOS 15.7.9 arm64",
  "compiler": "Nim 2.4.0 nim c -d:release --mm:arc; same binary/config/deps. Isolated nim ic failed twice with compiler rescheduling error, so classic backend used for both modes.",
  "sourceRevision": "881e74bf with range helper copied from working tree",
